  "question": {
    "text": "Two particles of masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> approach each other with different velocities. After collision, the particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> has velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;in their centre of mass frame. Velocity of particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;in the centre of mass frame is",
